# Spectra — Sortie

This file defines the mode this build ships and the one rule it settles: what a
mismatched shot does to the drone it hits. Everything else about a mismatched shot,
including that the bullet is consumed and destroys nothing, is in `specs/bands.md`.

## The mode

The build ships one playable mode, Sortie. Its entry on the title menu is `LAUNCH`,
the first item of `TITLE_ITEMS`, and `specs/ui.md` states the menu it sits in.

In Sortie the ship flies against wave after wave of the swarm, flipping bands to
match what it fires at and to shield what fires at it, clearing each stage and
pressing into faster ones until the last life is lost.

## A mismatched shot is wasted

A shot whose effective band is the opposite of the drone's leaves that drone exactly
as it was. Its phase, its position, its slot, its stored band, its band clock, its
shell, and its course are all unchanged, and it is neither redirected nor marked in
any way.

The shot adds nothing to the score and nothing to the resonance meter, and it plays
no cue of its own. Sortie adds no sound beside the nine `specs/ui.md` states.
